/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=()
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' https://cdn.jsdelivr.net; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://cdn.jsdelivr.net; img-src 'self' data:; font-src 'self' https://cdn.jsdelivr.net; connect-src 'self' https://logs.lindfors.no; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'self'; object-src 'none'

/blog/*.md
  Content-Type: text/markdown; charset=utf-8
  Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *

# The .md files are the negotiated representation of each post, also addressable
# directly. Cloudflare would otherwise serve them as application/octet-stream, which
# makes clients download rather than read them. CORS is open because these exist to
# be fetched by other people's tools.

# Notes on the CSP above.
#
# script-src has no 'unsafe-inline' and no nonce. Cloudflare Pages serves this file
# statically, so there is no per-request value to inject a nonce with, and hashes would
# have to be recomputed on every script edit. Every inline <script> and every
# onclick=/onload= attribute was moved into static/js/ instead, so plain 'self' works
# and stays correct. Do not reintroduce inline handlers -- they fail silently in the
# browser while looking fine in the build.
#
# cdn.jsdelivr.net is KaTeX, loaded only on pages that set extra.katex, with SRI hashes.
# It needs script-src, style-src and font-src (katex.min.css pulls its own fonts).
#
# style-src keeps 'unsafe-inline'. Zola's syntax highlighter emits per-token
# style="color:..." attributes on every code block, and style attributes cannot be
# covered by hashes. Removing it means switching Zola to class-based highlighting and
# shipping a theme stylesheet -- worth doing, but it changes rendered output, so it is
# not bundled into a security header change. script-src is where XSS is actually
# stopped; this is the honest limit of the current setup.
#
# connect-src 'self' covers the newsletter POST: newsletter_endpoint is /api/subscribe,
# same origin, proxied to the Worker.
#
# logs.lindfors.no is the OpenObserve RUM ingest, and only appears in connect-src: the
# SDK bundle itself is vendored into static/js/ (scripts/fetch-rum.sh), so script-src
# stays 'self'. It is gated on extra.rum.enabled in zola.toml -- the host is named here
# whether or not the scripts are shipped, because a header that has to be edited in
# lockstep with a config flag is a header that will be wrong once.
